PATCH 194: complete the mission-viewport 22dd handler sub-list 1 -- the interpreter now runs the whole
phase (0x23ea trig -> 0x41d0 op-0xc record -> 0x3fba crosshair -> 0x378e object render-walk -> 0x41ee ->
0x23ce terminate), the loop EXITS (word[0x450]=0), and 459a continues.  The ACCEPT cascade is CRASH-FREE
through the whole 22dd phase (was: trap-hang at 0x3fba after patch 193).

The mission handler-offset table at DGROUP:0x6c8e (dumped from re_out/fist_dat_image.bin) is, for the
d549=0x1e seed, the six-handler sub-list {0x23ea,0x41d0,0x3fba,0x378e,0x41ee,0x23ce}.  After patch 193
promoted 0x41d0 the cursor advanced to 0x3fba (a mid-entry that trapped).  This patch promotes/reconstructs
the remaining four, all asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00; si=word[0x1552]
src-geom / di=word[0x156a] dst-geom are DGROUP NEAR-OFFSETS -> the patch-186 base-loss class, rebased onto
g_mem+0x1c000+near_offset):

 * 0x3fba (crosshair-DRAW) + 0x40ec (crosshair-ERASE): plot/restore a 0xff mark into the dst-geom
   off-screen page at the src-geom-relative coord (rowtable word[0x794]; saved pixel word[0x6b76]; the
   page==word[0x722] branch wraps the write with the driver present methods far[0x159c]/[0x15a0]).  0x3fba
   advances the cursor FIRST.  (With the viewport geometry still uninitialised the two viewport-bounds
   checks early-return, so no pixel is drawn yet -- faithful clipping, crash-free.)
 * 0x41ee: `call 0x49b5 (already promoted, reads no input reg); addw 2,[0x4a86]`.
 * 0x23ce: the phase TERMINATOR: `call 0x40ec; orb 0x80,[0x1548]; word[0x450]=0; byte[0x154d]=0;
   cursor=word[0x4a88]`.  word[0x450]=0 makes the 22dd loop exit.
 * 0x378e (base-loss reconstruction, PRE-EXISTING function -- exposed now that 3fba advances the cursor
   to it): the mission-object RENDER-WALK.  begin far[0x6b0](ax=0xffff); loop { si=word[0x4b9e]; call near
   iterator [0x1630] (fills the 0x6bbe object struct, returns CF=done via the shim global g_fist_cf +
   updated si); if CF break; word[0x4b9e]=si; dl=byte[0x6bc2] (the object's render method-id); call near
   word[DGROUP: dl + 0x4b52] (the per-object render-method table) } end far[0x6b0]; addw 2,[0x4a86].
   Ghidra base-lost the method dispatch (`*(u16*)(word[0x6bc2]+0x4b52)` = a wild host-ptr deref -> SEGV)
   and folded the iterator CF; reconstructed instruction-faithful.  The iterator [0x1630] is installed at
   runtime (the walk terminates after dispatching each object's render method -- OBSERVED: 2 objects
   walked, render methods 0x0c06d/0x0c33c dispatched, then done -- so g_fist_cf is driven by the real
   iterator, not guessed).

OBSERVATION GATE (per doctrine -- render not yet verifiable): on the ACCEPT cascade (FIST_CASCADE=1, the
patch-172 3-click route, from repo root) there is NO SEGV and NO core; the 22dd handler traps
(0x03fba/0x0378e/0x041ee/0x023ce/0x041d0) are ALL GONE; the phase runs to its terminator, 378e walks the
object list dispatching each object's render method (the unpromoted per-object handlers 0x0c06d/0x0c33c
trap harmlessly -- the NEXT frontier: the per-object render dispatch -> the voxel raycaster), and execution
continues in the op-0x4c display-list present pump (steady state).  Structurally asm-faithful.

Behaviour-neutral for the 19 verify flows: every handler is reached only through the d548-gated 22dd loop
(d548==0 in the menu) with no direct callers, and the 378e/40ec base-loss fixes only change functions that
were WRONG (wild host-ptr derefs) and are reached only on the mission path.  verify.sh both stays 19/19;
default boot rc=0; mainmenu md5 3a6ff1c5 unchanged.  Sources stay pristine (re_out/fist.c 61453e42); fist.c
via build/.

